{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Kassapa","html":"<article id='thag1.82'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.82 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.82 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Navamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Nine </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kassapattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Kassapa </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Yena yena subhikkhāni, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Go, child, to any place </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sivāni abhayāni ca; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>where there’s plenty of food, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tena puttaka gacchassu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>where it’s safe and free of peril—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>mā sokāpahato bhavā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>may you not be overcome by sorrow! </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Kassapo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
